  "question": {
    "text": "The calculated spin only magnetic moments of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Cr</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msub><mi>CuF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BM</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;respectively, are&nbsp;(Atomic numbers of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cr</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>29</mn><mo>,</mo></math> respectively)",
